            "bodyHtml": "<p>Complete the notes below. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</p><div><div class=\"notes-title\"><strong>Office Design</strong></div><p class=\"sub-head\">Early 20th Century</p><ul><li>workers employed to do {{31}} were arranged in rows</li></ul><p class=\"sub-head\">1960s to present</p><p>Variations in design of open-plan offices:</p><ul><li>first, workers had individual {{32}}</li><li>later, they had cubicles with high or low {{33}}</li><li>nowadays, workers may have to {{34}} a work area</li></ul><p class=\"sub-head\">Survey results</p><p>Attitudes of employees to open-plan designs:</p><ul><li>there is a lack of {{35}} and {{36}}</li><li>they pose a risk to our {{37}} (staff records support this)</li></ul><p>Attitudes of employers to open-plan designs:</p><ul><li>they significantly reduce rent and {{38}} costs</li><li>they improve teamwork and communication</li><li>they can make {{39}} staff easier</li></ul><p>In reality, employees are unhappy and they are often distracted by the {{40}} the office.</p></div>",
